  <prompt>2026-08-28 dispatch attempt of `/provision-environment trial1 --batch runs/trial1-intake.json` HARD STOPped at SKILL Step 0.5b line ~337 constants sanity check. Deep audit surfaced 5 gap classes; 3 of them (Gap B recipe-contract, Gap C name-alignment-partial, Gap D&#8B;-forcing-function) are already scoped by tasks 206/207/208/209. This task 212 covers the remaining 4 gaps that would block dispatch even AFTER 206/207/208/209 land.

Full pre-dispatch readiness report + gap analysis: [`runs/pre-dispatch-readiness-gap-report.md`](../../runs/pre-dispatch-readiness-gap-report.md)

**Gap A — Populate `spaarke-constants.yaml per_env_constants.dev.*`**
- `containerTypeId`: null → look up SPE container-type GUID via SharePoint admin center OR app-only Graph query with `FileStorageContainerType.Selected` app permission. Operator identity (user-delegated) got 403 on `GET /beta/storage/fileStorage/containerTypes` — as expected; user-delegated does not carry this scope. Populate with real GUID. Container-type is `never_delete: true` per PRQ-T-01 owner directive 2026-08-24.
- `bffMultiTenantAppId`: null → CROSS-REFERENCES GAP D. If Gap D resolves as "use single-tenant dev BFF (existing app-reg `1e40baad-e065-4aea-a8d4-4b7ab273458c` = Spaarke BFF)", populate with that GUID + explanatory comment. If resolves as "register multi-tenant BFF for dev", populate with the new app-reg GUID after registration.

**Gap C — Correct `name_templates` against LIVE Azure state**
Verified 2026-08-28 discrepancies:
- `platformKvName: sprk-{env}-kv` → assumes `sprk-dev-kv` for dev; ACTUAL KV in `rg-spaarke-platform-dev` is `sprk-controlplane-dev-kv`. Change template to `sprk-controlplane-{env}-kv` OR introduce per-env override.
- BFF App Service search assumption in SKILL Step 0.5b line ~279 looks in `rg-spaarke-platform-dev` for `sprksharedprod-api*` OR `spaarke-bff-$env`; ACTUAL BFF `spaarke-bff-dev` lives in `rg-spaarke-dev` (different RG). Either add `bffAppServiceRg: rg-spaarke-{env}` per-env override to constants OR change SKILL Step 0.5b to search across RGs OR change constants to enumerate exact expected paths.
- `artifactsStorageName: sprk{env}artifacts` and `acrName: sprk{env}acr` — UNVERIFIED. Check via `az resource list --resource-group rg-spaarke-platform-dev` and correct or accept-as-not-yet-provisioned.

**Gap D — Model 1 shared multi-tenant BFF absent (ADR-028 tension, requires §6.5 escalation)**
ADR-028 line 229 mandates: "Model 1 — shared Spaarke environment (20+ customers; ONE shared multi-tenant BFF App Service + ONE shared BFF UAMI)". Deployed reality (verified 2026-08-28):
- Zero app-regs with `signInAudience != 'AzureADMyOrg'` in the Spaarke tenant (all 14 spaarke-* app-regs are single-tenant).
- `spaarke-bff-dev` App Service uses `1e40baad-e065-4aea-a8d4-4b7ab273458c` (Spaarke BFF) — single-tenant.
- The `trial1` dispatch's `tenantId=a221a95e-...` IS the Spaarke tenant, so this specific dispatch might sneak through end-to-end on the single-tenant BFF. But any real customer's tenantId will fail at H0.5 admin-consent.
- CLAUDE.md § MUST rules: "MUST NOT create per-customer Entra tenant; use one Spaarke tenant + one multitenant BFF app (spec.md §9.1 v3)". This is a codified MUST that the dev environment doesn't satisfy.

**§6.5 escalation MUST fire for this task**. Present the operator with the 3 documented paths (root CLAUDE.md §6.5):
- **Path A (project-scoped exception)**: dispatch trial1 (and any subsequent same-tenant test runs) against single-tenant dev BFF; document as ADR-028 project-scoped exception for `env=dev` only; register multi-tenant BFF for dev before ANY real-customer Model 1 dispatch. Pros: unblocks trial1 immediately. Cons: creates a landmine — real-customer dispatch WILL fail at H0.5 unless someone remembers this exception.
- **Path B (ADR amendment)**: amend ADR-028 to acknowledge dev tier does not require multi-tenant BFF (Model 1 is a shared-Spaarke-hosted-only design in dev). Pros: honest about reality. Cons: real customer would still need multi-tenant somewhere.
- **Path C (pivot to comply)**: dispatch is BLOCKED until multi-tenant BFF is registered for dev; file `spaarke-dev-multitenant-bff-registration-r1` follow-on project; work through Register-EntraAppRegistrations.ps1 in multi-tenant mode + verify H0.5 admin-consent flow end-to-end. Pros: fully compliant. Cons: adds an unknown amount of work before trial1 can dispatch (probably 4-8h + Microsoft-side admin consent latency).

**Gap E — H8 containerTypeId runtime source unknown**
L2 App Service (`spaarke-provisioning-controlplane-dev`) has 13 app settings — none reference SPE or ContainerType. `sprk-controlplane-dev-kv` KV search for `SPE` or `Container` returned nothing. But H8 (SPE container creation) and H13 (acceptance verification) need this value at runtime.

Investigate: `grep -rn "containerType\|ContainerType" src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/**/*H8*`. Options:
- (a) H8 reads from `IntakeParameters.NonSecretParameters.ContainerTypeId` → SKILL Step 4.0 payload MUST include `containerTypeId` in nonSecretParameters (currently doesn't). Add.
- (b) H8 reads from per-customer KV secret populated by H4 → verify secret name in H4 KV manifest OR add.
- (c) H8 reads from L2 App Service setting `SPE__ContainerTypeId` → add to L2 App Service settings via `az webapp config appsettings set`.
- (d) H8 reads from a hardcoded constant → refactor.

Document the actual answer + apply the fix. If it's (a), SKILL Step 4.0 payload block needs one-line addition. If (b) or (c), infrastructure fix. If (d), architectural code change.

**Sequencing constraint**: THIS task (212) must complete BEFORE task 207 (which extends the SKILL substitution block for `{containerTypeId}` — depends on Gap A being populated) AND BEFORE task 206 (which fixes recipe exit-1 semantics that will fire against real Gap E state). Full sequence: 212 → 206 → 207 → 208 → 209 → dispatch.</prompt>

  <role>Main-session operator (skill-directives + operator-config-file hot-path + §6.5 escalation authority).</role>

  <goal>All four sub-gaps resolved: Gap A populated, Gap C corrected against LIVE Azure state, Gap D §6.5 escalation surfaced + operator decision captured + applied, Gap E H8 runtime source documented + fix landed. Re-invoking `/provision-environment trial1 --batch runs/trial1-intake.json` progresses past Step 0.5b constants sanity check (may still HARD STOP downstream at task-206/207-scoped Gap B issues — that's expected + is 206/207's job to resolve).</goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Discovery is from the first live batch-mode dispatch attempt of task 186 on 2026-08-28. The dispatch was intended to be the clean E2E Model 1 stand-up. SESSION 14 had judged Class A parseability sufficient to "unblock task 186 dispatch," but that assessment overlooked the constants sanity check in SKILL Step 0.5b which fires BEFORE the placeholder-substitution loop (Session 14's Class B/C scope). This task 212 is the corrective — plus catches the two NEW findings (Gap D architectural absence + Gap E runtime unknown) that no prior session had surfaced.

      The 5 gaps + why-Fable-missed-them analysis is in [`runs/pre-dispatch-readiness-gap-report.md`](../../runs/pre-dispatch-readiness-gap-report.md). The root-cause is that isolated per-artifact review does not catch config-data-completeness, cross-artifact-naming-intersections, or architecture-vs-deployed-state gaps. A dry-dispatch integration test at Fable-time would catch all four Gap-B/C/D/E classes. That amendment to the Fable process is filed separately (see §6.5 output of this task for the follow-on POML pointer).
    </background>
